## Methodology to developing xgboost

Description
I have two shapefiles namely (points_of_presence and points_of absence). 
- points_of_presence: These contain data on where vineyards exist
- points_of_absence: These contain data on where there are currently no vineyards

Potential steps in model creation
- Installation of xgboost library in Python on vs-code
- Export my points data to csv or tables from arc gis pro 
    - These were seperated by semi-colons';' and not commas ','
- Read in the data as csv (presence_df and absence_df)
    - View data
    - Assing 1 to presence_df and 0 to absence_df
    - Combine the data into one dataframe
    - Check for nulls
    - Convert data to float or double (because the values in the data are seperated by commas ',' their data type is object )
    - Data description
    - Interpolate if there are null values in the datasets (presence and absence)
    - Data visualisation
- Hyper-parameter optimisation
- Model training


